{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"111451","commit":"b3d2bb0be10cd7cb61700efa417de214ac6a2aa3","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"`prettyPrintList` calls `Object::toString` on every element without a null guard. If any element in the array or list is `null`, this will throw a `NullPointerException` at the exact moment the test is trying to produce a diagnostic message. A small safeguard such as `list.stream().map(e -\u003e String.valueOf(e)).collect(...)` would make the error reporting robust.","nodes":[{"id":"modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/datastreams/logsdb/qa/matchers/Matcher.java-modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/datastreams/logsdb/qa/matchers/Matcher.java--4093:4261","promptId":"#YK1DQ","srcPath":"modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/datastreams/logsdb/qa/matchers/Matcher.java","dstPath":"modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/datastreams/logsdb/qa/matchers/Matcher.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4093,"endPos":4261,"startLine":119,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":121,"endLineOffset":5,"length":169}]}]},{"comment":"The `createSettings` method applies `commonSettingsConsumer` *after* `settingsConsumer`, meaning common settings can silently override any value set by the specific (baseline/contender) consumer. In the current code there is no overlap, so this is harmless, but if a future subclass sets a value in `baselineSettings`/`contenderSettings` that `commonSettings` also sets, the common value will win — which is the opposite of the more conventional \"defaults first, overrides last\" pattern. Consider applying `commonSettingsConsumer` first and `settingsConsumer` second, or at minimum adding a brief comment documenting the intended precedence.","nodes":[{"id":"modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearch/datastreams/logsdb/qa/AbstractChallengeRestTest.java-modules/data-streams/src/javaRestTest/java/org/elasticsearc